LRC14 TILING/SOLID RECURSION ATLAS
========================================================================

A. Regular {p,q} curvature
------------------------------------------------------------------------
delta = 2/p + 2/q - 1.  Sphere: delta>0, plane: delta=0.
tetrahedron   {p,q}={3,3}  delta= 1/3  (V,E,F)=(4,6,4)  self-dual; K4/tournament object
cube          {p,q}={4,3}  delta= 1/6  (V,E,F)=(8,12,6)  dual octahedron; tournament cube space
octahedron    {p,q}={3,4}  delta= 1/6  (V,E,F)=(6,12,8)  dual cube; arc-coordinate space
dodecahedron  {p,q}={5,3}  delta=1/15  (V,E,F)=(20,30,12)  dual icosahedron; quotient-dual surface
icosahedron   {p,q}={3,5}  delta=1/15  (V,E,F)=(12,30,20)  dual dodecahedron; G5 f-vector surface

triangular {p,q}={3,6}  delta=0  dual=hexagonal   p*q=18  six triangles around each vertex
square     {p,q}={4,4}  delta=0  dual=square      p*q=16  self-dual grid; m^2 square subdivisions
hexagonal  {p,q}={6,3}  delta=0  dual=triangular  p*q=18  three hexagons around each vertex

B. Square, triangular, and hexagonal recursion numbers
------------------------------------------------------------------------
square self m^2:      [1, 4, 9, 16, 25, 36, 49, 64, 81, 100]
triangle self m^2:    [1, 4, 9, 16, 25, 36, 49, 64]  (2-edge step gives 4, then 16)
centered hex clusters:[1, 7, 19, 37, 61, 91, 127, 169]  (side 2 gives 7 cells)
triangle <-> hex '6': local incidence/duality, not a lattice index: {3,6} <-> {6,3}.

